+# Pak Edu RAG - Class 9 Physics tutor (Lahore Board)
+
+A retrieval-augmented study assistant for the Punjab Textbook Board Class 9 Physics
+book and Lahore Board past papers (2023-2024). Students ask in English or
+Roman Urdu/Hinglish; answers are grounded in retrieved textbook / past-paper text
+and every answer lists the sources it used.
+
+## How it works
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+    subgraph Offline["Offline pipeline"]
+        A[Scanned PDFs] -->|Gemini vision OCR<br/>pdf_to_text.py| B[page .txt files]
+        B -->|chunk_and_tag.py<br/>chunk_past_papers.py| C[chunks.jsonl<br/>+ chapter / page / year / question type]
+        C -->|build_vectordb.py<br/>BGE-small embeddings| D[(ChromaDB)]
+        C --> E[BM25 index]
+    end
+    subgraph Online["Online (app.py -> qa.py)"]
+        Q[Student question] --> L{language?}
+        L -->|rewrite / translate to English| R[standalone query]
+        R --> F[filters: chapter, source, question type]
+        F --> DS[dense search]
+        F --> BS[BM25 search]
+        D --> DS
+        E --> BS
+        DS --> RRF[Reciprocal Rank Fusion]
+        BS --> RRF
+        RRF --> X[cross-encoder re-rank]
+        X --> G[Gemini answer<br/>with [Source n] citations]
+        G --> U[Gradio chat + sources list]
+    end
+```
+
+* **Hybrid retrieval** - dense (`BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5` in ChromaDB) and sparse (BM25)
+  are two independent retrievers fused with RRF, then re-ranked by a small cross-encoder
+  (`Xenova/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2`, optional and fail-soft).
+* **Relevance gates** - a dense distance threshold and a BM25 minimum score keep
+  out-of-scope questions from retrieving anything, so the tutor can refuse honestly.
+* **Metadata filters** - chapter, source type (textbook / past paper) and question type
+  (MCQ / short / long), set from dropdowns or detected in the question text.
+* **Query rewriting** - follow-ups ("explain them too") become standalone questions and
+  Roman-Urdu questions are translated to English before retrieval.
+* **Grounded answers** - the prompt requires `[Source n]` citations; MCQ answers must say
+  whether they come from the sources or were solved by the tutor (past papers have no answer key).
+
+## Setup
+
+```bash
+python -m venv venv && source venv/bin/activate
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+cp .env.example .env            # then put your own GEMINI_API_KEY in .env
+```
+
+The OCR step (`pdf_to_text.py`) additionally needs poppler (`sudo apt install poppler-utils`).
+
+### Build and run
+
+```bash
+# 1. textbook chunks (re-run after changing the chunker or the OCR text)
+python chunk_and_tag.py          # -> data/.../textbook_chunks.jsonl
+
+# 2. past-paper chunks (chunk_past_papers.py does NOT add chapters; the next two steps do, via Gemini)
+python chunk_past_papers.py      # -> data/.../past_paper_chunks.jsonl
+python tag_chapters_pastpapers.py
+python fix_none_chapters.py      # retries any chunk that still has chapter=None
+
+# 3. embeddings (safe to re-run; rebuilds the collection)
+python build_vectordb.py         # -> ./chroma_db
+
+python app.py                    # Gradio UI at http://127.0.0.1:7860
+```
+
+## Evaluation
+
+```bash
+python eval_retrieval.py --bm25-only   # no vector DB / model download needed
+python eval_retrieval.py               # full ablation -> eval/results/ablation.md
+python eval_generation.py --limit 20   # LLM-judge faithfulness + refusal (uses API quota)
+pytest                                 # offline unit tests (no API key, no model download)
+RUN_LLM_TESTS=1 pytest -m llm          # live grounding tests
+```
+
+`eval/gold_set.jsonl` holds 66 answerable queries (43 definitions, 6 paraphrases,
+10 Roman-Urdu, 7 past-paper lookups) and 12 out-of-scope queries. A chunk counts as relevant
+when it contains the query's verbatim `answer_phrases`, so the evaluation survives
+re-chunking. Metrics: Hit@1, Hit@5, MRR@5, nDCG@5, Precision@5, and the false-retrieval
+rate on out-of-scope queries.
+
+### Results
+
+Paste the output of `python eval_retrieval.py` here (it is written to `eval/results/ablation.md`):
+
+| Configuration | Hit@1 | Hit@5 | MRR@5 | nDCG@5 | P@5 | False retrieval (out-of-scope) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| BM25 only | 0.50 | 0.74 | 0.600 | 0.630 | 0.17 | 0.42 |
+| Dense only | _run_ | | | | | |
+| Hybrid (old: BM25 gated by dense) | _run_ | | | | | |
+| Hybrid (RRF) | _run_ | | | | | |
+| Hybrid (RRF) + reranker | _run_ | | | | | |
+
+## Known limitations
+
+* The embedding model is English-only; Roman-Urdu questions rely on the LLM rewrite step.
+* Chunks never cross page boundaries, so a definition split over two pages is split in two.
+* MCQ answers that are not in the sources are solved by the LLM (and labelled as such).
+* The gold set was written from the OCR text by one author; extend it before drawing strong conclusions.
+
+## Data and copyright
+
+The OCR text and chunks are derived from Punjab Textbook Board books and Lahore Board
+past papers. Check that you may redistribute them before publishing the repository
+(see the commented `data/` line in `.gitignore`).
+
+## Project layout
+
+| File | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `config.py` | paths, model names, thresholds, API key loading (`.env`) |
+| `pdf_to_text.py` | PDF pages -> text with Gemini vision |
+| `chunk_and_tag.py`, `chunk_past_papers.py`, `tag_chapters_pastpapers.py`, `fix_none_chapters.py` | chunking + metadata |
+| `build_vectordb.py` | embeddings -> ChromaDB |
+| `hybrid_search.py` | dense + BM25 + RRF + re-ranking |
+| `qa.py` | language detection, query rewriting, prompt, answer / stream |
+| `app.py` | Gradio UI |
+| `eval_retrieval.py`, `eval_generation.py`, `eval/gold_set.jsonl` | evaluation |
+| `tests/` | pytest suite |
